        {
          "id": 1181313162,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "An example on how to keep track of the overflow counter on a per packet number basis can be found in the packet-mbim.c dissector. Each time a new MBIM OPEN message is received (that can be seen as an overflow of the fragment_id in LAPDm context) the new open_count value and the corresponding packet number is stored in a conversation tree:\n<pre>\nif (!PINFO_FD_VISITED(pinfo)) {\n                    mbim_conv->open_count++;\n                    wmem_tree_insert32(mbim_conv->open, pinfo->num, GUINT_TO_POINTER(mbim_conv->open_count));\n                }\n</pre>\nThen for a given packet, the applicable local open_count value is retrieved with:\n<pre>\nopen_count = GPOINTER_TO_UINT(wmem_tree_lookup32_le(mbim_conv->open, pinfo->num));\n</pre>\nI guess a similar approach could be used here.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
