        {
          "id": 1181407175,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Since this is my first time dealing with wireshark's code, I have several questions:\n* Arbitrary access - does wireshark reanalyse a specific packet on select? From what I saw the `fragment_add_seq_next` function is caching the result (if fd->visited) so there aren't any arbitrary access problems.\n* Are there dissector tests I can write in order to make sure these cases are covered?\n* Would you prefer further changes in this PR to be amended or to be committed in another commit?\n\nThanks a lot for the CR, I am looking forward to your reply on the arbitrary access point.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8174449,
            "username": "matan1008",
