        {
          "id": 1181430894,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The first pass (!fd->visited) is performed in order (by increasing packet number). All subsequent access to a packet can be out of order (that's what happens when you select a random packet in the GUI).\n\nAfter checking the code, it appears that lapdm_last_n_s_map is only used during the first pass, which was not obvious when seeing your change in GitLab GUI (it is put in a code part that is executed whatever the pass number), thus my comment. But I agree it is not relevant after a closer look. For clarity it might make sense to add a !PINFO_FD_VISITED(pinfo) test like all the other accesses to lapdm_last_n_s_map map.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
